Logs the missing registry of IANA's enterprise numbers at the level of
-v, not as an error. ipmitool reads the registry at every start to name
the manufacturer of a BMC, and says "IANA PEN registry open failed" on
the standard error when the file is not there. The port does not ship
the registry: the build must not download it, and a copy pinned in the
port would age. Without it ipmitool names the manufacturers its own
table holds and shows the others by number, which every command still
works with, so a start with no registry is not an error to show.

--- a/lib/ipmi_strings.c
+++ b/lib/ipmi_strings.c
@@ -1515,7 +1515,7 @@
 		 */
 		in = fopen(IANADIR PATH_SEPARATOR IANA_PEN_REGISTRY, "r");
 		if (!in) {
-			lperror(LOG_ERR, "IANA PEN registry open failed");
+			lperror(LOG_INFO, "IANA PEN registry open failed");
 			return -1;
 		}
 	}
